From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:00:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] KitKat UI P18.4: hide the QS build-text footer (donor
 QS had none)

qs_footer_impl (modern build/version footer) rendered 48dp+8dp above
the brightness slider inside QSPanel - the dead band between the
48dp shade header and the slider. 4.4 had no such footer; hide it in
QSPanel.onFinishInflate so the slider sits directly under the header
clearance.
---
 .../SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSPanel.java     | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSPanel.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSPanel.java
index 86dc225f3173..a321e6a4dac2 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSPanel.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSPanel.java
@@ -437,6 +437,14 @@ public class QSPanel extends LinearLayout {
     protected void onFinishInflate() {
         super.onFinishInflate();
         mFooter = findViewById(R.id.qs_footer);
+        // KitKat UI P18.4: the 4.4 QS panel had NO build/version-text footer
+        // above the tile grid (or the brightness slider). Hide it so the
+        // slider sits directly under the 48dp header clearance
+        // (qs_panel_padding_top) - the dead band it left (48dp height +
+        // 8dp bottom margin) was the gap between header and brightness bar.
+        if (mFooter != null) {
+            mFooter.setVisibility(View.GONE);
+        }
     }
 
     private void updateHorizontalLinearLayoutMargins() {
